       H(x,2t) &,\text{ if } 0 \le t \le \frac{1}{2}\\
       H'(x,2t-1) &, \text{ if } \frac{1}{2} \le t \le 1
     \end{array}
   \right.\\$

is a homotopy from $f$ to $j$. I can see that this is a transitive property, but I can't seem to find a way to show that this mapping is continuous. I know to show continuity I must show that $V \in T' \Rightarrow F^{-1}(V) \in T$, but I can't see how to show that $F^{-1}(V) \in T.$

